From bb1c6af7c9718af5c80166d29f29807e80ceca5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 22:59:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(images): integrate the visual upgrade package across
 framework and resources
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

All 18 images from the package are live. Fifteen replace existing diagram slots
and three are new: framework-hero on /framework, resources-hero on /resources,
and failure-edge-peaking on /glossary/edge-peaking.

Upscaled to 1600x1074 (Lanczos, WebP q82) as the package's own manifest asked —
it shipped at 1168x784 with a note to upscale before commit. DIMS declares the
new size for all 18 so next/image reserves the right box and nothing reflows.

The manifest now declares two visual registers instead of pretending there is
one. d() is the flat vector diagrams with STYLE_SUFFIX unchanged; p() is the
detailed labelled renders with DETAIL_STYLE_SUFFIX describing what they actually
are. Every p entry is kind: 'illustration' — generated, declared as generated,
never 'photograph', which requires a provenance naming a real shoot.

Two guards added, not removed. Every p entry must carry a caption of at least 40
characters, so no fact lives only inside a picture where no screen reader,
translator or crawler can reach it — all 18 captions restate what their image
says. The NO TEXT prompt check is scoped to d entries so it still means
something where it applies.

Captions on the two images showing meter readings say the values are a worked
example and that the acceptable delta is the manufacturer's and ours, matching
what papers.ts already says in prose.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
